# Cheatsheet

Everything a song can say, a line of code for each.
[From a note to a song](first_song.md) builds a first song step by step, and [the notation](notation.md) describes each function in full.
In the examples `music` is any music, and lengths are in beats.

## Sounds
{: .col-2}

### A note

```elixir
note(:a4, 1.5)
note(:a4, 1.5, vel: 0.8, release: 2)
rest(1)
```

A pitch and a length, then options for the synth.
`rest` is silence.

### A chord

```elixir
note([:c4, :e4, :g4], 2)
note(chord(:e3, :minor), 1, strum: 0.05)
```

A list of pitches sounds at once.
`strum:` starts each note that long after the one below.

### A drum's stroke

```elixir
hit(vel: 0.5)
```

A drum has its own pitch, and a hit takes no time.

### Pitches

```elixir
pitch(:c4)
pitch("fs3")
pitch(:eb3) + 12
```

A letter, `s` for a sharp or `b` for a flat, and an octave.
A pitch is also a number, 60 for C4, so it takes plain arithmetic.

## Joining
{: .col-2}

### One after another

```elixir
seq(c4: 1, e4: 1, g4: 2, r: 1)
seq([music, rest(2), music])
seq(1..4, fn bar -> note(60 + bar, 1) end)
```

### At once

```elixir
together([seq(c5: 2, b4: 2), note(:e4, 4)])
together([:c4, :e4], fn name -> note(name, 2) end)
```

It lasts as long as its longest item.

### Again

```elixir
repeat(music, 4)
repeat(music)
```

With no count it plays until mx stops, and holds the whole song.

### At a beat

```elixir
at([{0, hit()}, {1.5, hit(vel: 0.5)}], 4)
delay(music, 7)
```

`at` starts each item at its beat, in music of 4 beats.
`delay` is the music after 7 beats of silence.

### Moved, and shaped

```elixir
transpose(music, 12)
each(music, vel: 0.8)
slur(seq(a4: 1, c5: 1, e5: 2), slide: 0.1)
```

`each` gives options to every note that has none of its own.
`slur` joins notes into one that changes pitch, with no new attack.

### Measured

```elixir
beats(music)
```

## Patterns
{: .col-2}

### A word to a step

```elixir
steps(~MX"g4:2 _ g4 bb4:2 _ a4 | g4:4 - -", 0.25, vel: 0.8)
```

| Word | Is |
|---|---|
| `g4` | that note, for one step |
| `_` | a step of silence |
| `-` | the word before, a step longer |
| `g4:2` `g4:1.5` `g4:1/3` | a length in steps |
| `g5/b4` | notes together |
| `[f f]` | words sharing one step |
| `~g2` | a glide from the note before, not struck again |
| `>g4` | accented, as `accent:` says |
| `^d6` | a grace note, taking no step |
| `\|` | a bar line, only for reading |

### A character to a step

```elixir
steps(~MX"9... 9... 9..5 9.7."s, 0.25)
steps(~MX"ccoc ccoc"s, 0.25, strokes: [o: [vel: 0.75], c: [vel: 0.5]])
```

| Character | Is |
|---|---|
| `x` | a hit |
| `1` to `9` | a hit at that level |
| `.` | silence |
| a letter | a stroke named in `strokes:` |

### What `steps` takes

```elixir
steps(~MX"o >o c", 0.25, strokes: [o: [vel: 0.6], c: [vel: 0.4]], accent: 0.3)
steps(~MX"S R g", 0.5, words: [S: :d4, R: :e4, g: :f4])
steps(~MX"1.2.3."s, 0.25, notes: [:g4, :a4, :bb4])
steps(~MX"x..x"s, 0.25, sample: {:sonic_pi, :bd_haus})
steps(~MX"c4 ^d4 e4 ~g4", 0.5, grace: 0.06, slide: 0.3)
```

`strokes:` gives a letter its options, `words:` gives a word its pitch, and `notes:` tunes the digits.
`accent:` is a number added to vel, or a list of options.

### Joining patterns

```elixir
steps([~MX"9...9..."s, ~MX"9..59.7."s], 0.25)
steps(~MX"c4 e4" ++ ~MX"g4:2", 0.5)
```

A list of patterns plays as one bar after another.

## Feel
{: .col-2}

### Tables of timing and loudness

```elixir
feel(music, step: 0.25, push: [0, 0.035, 0, 0.035], lean: [1, 0.7, 0.85, 0.7])
feel(music, step: 0.25, loose: 0.01, touch: 0.1)
```

A number for each step, going round.
`push:` is how much later the step plays, and `lean:` multiplies its vel.
`loose:` and `touch:` are small random changes, the same on every load.

### Any rule

```elixir
swing(music, fn beat -> beat + 0.02 end)
```

Each note starts at the beat the function returns.

## Parts
{: .col-2}

### A part

```elixir
part(:keys, music, synth: :piano, fx: [echo: [phase: 0.75], reverb: [decay_seconds: 3.2]], defaults: [amp: 0.55])
```

One player: a name, its music, a synth, its effects in order, and options for its notes.
The synth is `:tri` unless given.

### Changing a sound while it plays

```elixir
change(:pad, cutoff: 110, cutoff_slide: 8)
change({:pad, :reverb}, mix: 0)
note(:a4, 4, changes: [{1, note: :c5, note_slide: 0.1}])
```

`change` reaches a part's sounding notes, or one of its effects.
`changes:` is a note's own: a beat into it, and what changes there.

### Synths

| Family | Synths |
|---|---|
| Keys | `piano` `electric_piano` `organ` `harmonium` `accordion` |
| Plucked | `guitar` `electric_guitar` `electric_bass` `bandolim` `cavaquinho` `harp` `sitar` `pluck` `tanpura` `berimbau` |
| Bowed | `violin` `viola` `cello` `double_bass` |
| Winds | `flute` `oboe` `clarinet` `bassoon` `tenor_sax` `trumpet` `trombone` `horn` `tuba` `brass` |
| Mallets | `marimba` `vibraphone` `xylophone` `glockenspiel` `timpani` |
| Waves | `tri` `saw` `square` `pulse` `supersaw` `fm` `acid` `deep_bass` `noise` |
| Drums | `kick` `snare` `closed_hihat` `open_hihat` `clap` `cowbell` `surdo` `cajon` and [many more](instruments.md#drums) |

### Effects

`reverb` `echo` `ping_pong` `chorus` `flanger` `phaser` `tremolo` `slicer` `wobble` `distortion` `bitcrusher` `compressor` `limiter` `eq` `lpf` `hpf` `bpf` `rlpf` `pan` `level`

Every effect takes `amp`, `mix` and `pre_amp`.
[Instruments](instruments.md) lists each synth's and effect's options.

## The song
{: .col-2}

### A script

```elixir
import Mx

melody = seq(c4: 1, e4: 1, g4: 2)

song(tempo: 72, music: part(:lead, melody, synth: :flute))
```

### A module

```elixir
defmodule Paredao do
  use Mx.Song, tempo: 92, key: :gm, meter: 4

  part :kick, synth: :kick
  part :bass, synth: :double_bass, defaults: [amp: 0.5]

  kit :drums, k: [part: :kick, vel: 0.9]

  def song, do: form([intro: 1, beat: 2], &section/1)

  defp section(:intro), do: only(band(), :bass)
  defp section(:beat), do: band()

  defp band, do: together([kit(:drums, ~MX"k _ _ k", 1), part(:bass, note(:g1, 4))])
end
```

Parts are declared once and played by name.
A kit plays beside the parts, since its strokes go to several of them.
`key:` and `meter:` are for scores and drawings, and do not change what plays.

### Sections and form

```elixir
seq([intro, verse, verse])
form([a: 2, b: 2, a: 1], fn section -> note(section, 4) end)
```

The items of the outermost `seq` are the sections.
A saved file takes over when the section playing ends.
`form` gives the order and the number of times, and calls a function for each.

### Who sits out

```elixir
without(band, [:kick, :bass])
only(band, :bell)
```

The music with parts left out, lasting as long as before.

### Kits

```elixir
kit :pandeiro,
  o: [part: :pandeiro_thumb, vel: 0.75],
  f: [part: :pandeiro_jingles, vel: 0.5],
  of: [:o, :f]

kit(:pandeiro, ~MX"o f >of f", 0.25, accent: [vel: 0.9])
```

Declared in a module: one pattern played across several parts, each stroke naming its part.

### Tempo

```elixir
seq([tempo(100), verse, tempo(140), chorus])
tempo(130, over: 16)
```

For every part, from the beat where it is written.

## Recordings
{: .col-2}

### One recording

```elixir
sample("kick.wav", 1)
sample({:sonic_pi, :bd_haus}, 1)
sample({:github, "owner/repo", "main", "kick.wav"}, 1)
```

A file of your own, a collection mx knows by name, or a public repository.

### Cut and fitted

```elixir
sample({:sonic_pi, :loop_amen}, 4, beats: 4)
sample({:sonic_pi, :loop_amen}, 0.5, slices: 8, slice: 3)
sample({:sonic_pi, :loop_amen}, 2, rate: -1, start: 0.5, finish: 1)
```

`beats:` fits the recording to the tempo.
It also takes `from:` and `to:` in seconds, `normalize:`, `amp:` and `pan:`.

### An instrument from a folder

```elixir
mbira = sampled({:vcsl, "Idiophones/Plucked Idiophones/Kalimba, Kenya"})

part(:mbira, music, synth: mbira)
```

Each note plays the nearest recorded key, at a strength chosen by its vel.

### Collections

`:sonic_pi` `:vcsl` `:vsco` `:salamander` `:mridangam` `:virtuosity_drums`, and the instruments of FreePats and Karoryfer.
[The notation](notation.md#collections) lists them.

```sh
mx samples download sonic_pi
```

## Loops and live
{: .col-2}

### A loop

```elixir
loop(4, fn pass, _inputs ->
  note(ring([:c4, :e4, :g4], pass), 4)
end)
```

Music worked out again on every pass, each lasting 4 beats.
`ring` is the item at an index, going round.

### Inputs

```elixir
loop(1, fn _pass, inputs ->
  note(:c2, 1, cutoff: (inputs.cc[74] || 64) / 127 * 60 + 50)
end)
```

`inputs.cc`, `inputs.notes`, `inputs.osc` and `inputs.values` hold what has arrived.

### Played live

```elixir
loop(fn trigger, _inputs -> note(trigger.note, 1) end, on: :midi_note, grid: 1)
```

A pass each time something arrives: `:midi_note`, `:midi_cc` or `{:osc, "/hit"}`.
`grid:` waits for the beat.

### Shared values

```elixir
set(:root, :f2)
```

Set in one loop, and read by every loop as `inputs.values[:root]` from its next pass.

### MIDI and OSC out

```elixir
midi(:c3, 1, velocity: 70)
midi_cc(74, 64)
osc("/flash", [1])
```

A part's `midi:` names its port, and the song's `osc_to:` and `osc_from:` name the addresses.

### Live audio

```elixir
song(tempo: 90, live_audio: [mic: [amp: 0.8, fx: [reverb: [mix: 0.3]]]], music: part(:pad, note(:c3, 8)))
```

A microphone through mx's effects.
Use headphones.

## Helpers
{: .col-2}

### Chords and scales

| Call | Is |
|---|---|
| `chord(:a3, :minor7)` | `[57, 60, 64, 67]` |
| `chord("Am7", from: :d4)` | `[69, 72, 76, 79]` |
| `scale(:e3, :minor_pentatonic)` | `[52, 55, 57, 59, 62, 64]` |
| `chord_at(~MX"D7 G", 2, 2)` | the chord a chart names at a beat |

Chords: `major` `minor` `major6` `minor6` `major7` `minor7` `dom7` `dom9` `dom7_flat9` `dim` `dim7` `half_dim7` `aug` `sus2` `sus4`

Scales: `major` `minor` `dorian` `mixolydian` `harmonic_minor` `major_pentatonic` `minor_pentatonic` `blues` `chromatic`

### Tunes and chords

| Call | Is |
|---|---|
| `intervals([60, 64, 67])` | `[4, 3]` |
| `melody(60, [4, 3, -2])` | `[60, 64, 67, 65]` |
| `nearest(65, chord(:c4, :major))` | `64` |
| `below(76, chord(:a4, :minor7))` | `72` |
| `voice(chord(:g2, :major6), from: 62, to: 73)` | `[62, 64, 67, 71]` |
| `fit(scale(:a4, :minor), chord(:e4, :dom7))` | the scale moved to hold the chord |

### Numbers

| Call | Is |
|---|---|
| `cents(386)` | `3.86` semitones |
| `ratio(5 / 4)` | `3.86` semitones |
| `ring([60, 64, 67], 4)` | `64` |
| `clamp(12, 2, 11)` | `11` |

### Chance

| Call | Is |
|---|---|
| `pick([60, 63, 67])` | one of them |
| `chance(0.45)` | true about 45 times in 100 |
| `between(0.6, 0.95)` | a number in that range |

Seeded from the song file, so a song plays the same notes each time it loads.

## Commands
{: .col-2}

### Play

```sh
mx play song.exs
mx play song.exs --record take.wav
mx play song.exs --render song.wav
mx play song.exs --render song.wav --seconds 60
```

`--record` writes what you hear, and `--render` writes the song without playing it.

### Look without listening

```sh
mx print song.exs
mx print song.exs --pass 4
```

Each part's notes with their beats, as text.
It is the quickest check that a song says what you meant.

### Scores

```sh
mx import score.mxl --tempo 72
mx export song.exs --time 6/8 --key d
mx hum hum.wav --tempo 90
```

### The rest

```sh
mx devices
mx samples download vcsl
mx video song.wav
mx help play
```
